{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each element stands in a tower of levels, one more with probability 1\/4, so a search skips","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ahead on the upper levels and finishes on the bottom one. Lookup, insertion and removal take","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":") expected time, with no rebalancing. Every link also records how many elements it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"passes, so the elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"like an array: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"list[0]"},{"text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index costs O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var numbers: SkipList = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","numbers.insert(4)","Array(numbers)                \/\/ [1, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9]","numbers.lowerBound(5)         \/\/ 3, the index of 5","numbers[1]                    \/\/ 3"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tower heights come from a random number generator given at creation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The list draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heights as its original."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The elements and their towers live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the list holds fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than 2³¹ − 1 elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/skiplists\/skiplist"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a skip list: sorted linked lists stacked in levels, each level a random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sample of the one below, searched from the top level down (Pugh, 1990)."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/LayersView-swift.struct"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/init()","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/init(_:using:)","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/init(using:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instanc